    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d524">

                <pb facs="0966" n="952" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg952"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.CC/12–2744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Donnelly</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-27T20:00:00-03:00">December 27,
                            1944—8 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4546. Department’s 3733, December 18, 7 p.m., and Embassy’s 3754, October 18, 6
                        p.m.<anchor n="79" xml:id="d524-f1"/> Velloso<anchor n="80" xml:id="d524-f2"
                    /> said to me today that the Brazilian <pb facs="0967" n="953" xml:id="pg953"/>
                    Government obviously prefers and considers that it is entitled to a permanent
                    seat on the Security Council but if it cannot be arranged that Brazil should
                    receive one of the first non-permanent seats. I believe that Brazil would be
                    satisfied with the latter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Donnelly</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d524-f1" n="79" xml:id="d524-f1-content">
                <p>Latter not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d524-f2" n="80" xml:id="d524-f2-content">
                <p>Pedro Leão Velloso, Acting Foreign Minister of Brazil.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
